# Topic Index

All topic files live in `.cursor/rules/topics/`. Read the relevant file before working on a feature area.

---

## Navigation & Pathfinding

- **NavMesh areas** (pathfinding, cost modifiers, area types) → `navmesh-areas.mdc`
- **NavMesh Bake Orchestrator** (provider protocol, rebake lifecycle, registered providers) → `bake-orchestrator.mdc`
- **Dual-mode NavMesh** (walking + wheelchair cached handles, instant mode switch, `navmesh_override` threading, orchestrator fan-out) → `navmesh-dual-mode.mdc`
- **NavMesh dev overlays** (`younite.navmesh_dev_overlays_extension`, dev stream only: full active mesh USD overlay + walking/wheelchair stair diff; Dev Tools toggles, `navmeshDebug*` / `accessibilityDiff*` events, world-state keys, `navmesh_route_bridge`, `navmeshDualBakeComplete`) → `navmesh-dev-overlays.mdc`
- **NavMesh shortest path package** (split Python modules under `scripts/navmesh_shortest_path/`: pathfinding, metrics, FP visualization; unchanged import path) → `navmesh-shortest-path-package.mdc`
- **NavMesh path refinement** (XZ straightening, Laplacian smoothing, threaded pipeline, ground snap) → `navmesh-path-refinement.mdc`
- **Route end flag** (cosmetic flag marker placed 50 cm before the polyline endpoint on every drawn FP sphere-trail route, asset-agnostic single-shot session-layer authoring, replaceable asset under `data/Assets/Flag/`, fallback green sphere when cache empty) → `route-end-flag.mdc`
- **RouteComposer** (unified A→B planner across NavMesh islands + OSM, ComposedRoute with polyline + per-segment speeds, used by directions panel and bird-eye preview) → `route-composer.mdc`
- **Waypoint routing** (corridor `nav_waypoint_*` graph, ring + branches, `plan_route()`, `plan_route_to_position` for POIs, via-points, `_best_ring_index` wall-ratio heuristic) → `waypoint-routing.mdc`
- **Turn-by-turn navigation** (polyline guide, RDP simplification, turn detection, seat pill) → `navigation-turn-by-turn.mdc`
- **Route measurement** (distance/time, move-to-x, routes to exits) → `route-measurement.mdc`
- **Bird's-eye route overlay** (NavMesh path → RDP → per-frame projection → SVG polyline, corridor waypoint support) → `bird-eye-route.mdc`
- **Bird-eye map controls** (drag-pan "grab the world", cinematic camera tilt while panels are open, endpoint icon swap, inert-backdrop rule, `birdEyePanFocusWorld` pan-to-target) → `bird-eye-map-controls.mdc`
- **Live transit overlay** (Västtrafik Planera Resa v4 `/positions`, USD cubes, `transitLiveOverlayStatus` + dev vehicle list, `TRANSIT_LIVE_*` env; Kit: `younite.open_data_live_extension`) → `transit-live-overlay.mdc`
- **OSM POI overlay (baked)** (`export_osm_pois.py`, `osm_pois_gbg.json`, dev IoT category toggle + `iotOsmPois*` markers; web uses shared `iotShared` list shell on mobile; complements live transit with static stops) → `osm-poi-overlay.mdc`
- **Bird-eye pin anywhere** (focalLength zoom, click-anywhere pin with magnet snap inside NavMesh / OSM node outside, directions hand-off to RouteComposer for unified multi-leg planning, cached polyline replayed for Play/Pause) → `bird-eye-pin-anywhere.mdc`
- **Seat navigation** (seat pipeline: `extract_cad_seats.py`, optional `postprocess_wheelchair_wc_to_row6.py`, instancer, lookup, `build_seat_hierarchy.py` / web `seat_hierarchy.json`; walking + wheelchair CU cascade; auto-move; highlighting; layout variants; arrival) → `seat-navigation.mdc`
- **OSM city navigation** (Dijkstra over baked graph: roads + railway, `generate_roads` + Kit terrain bake, `tram`/`train` modes for transit) → `osm-navigation.mdc`
- **OSM route overlay (dev)** (translucent glass-tinted walk-graph mesh on the session layer, click-to-walk along visible routes via direct `navmeshRouteWaypoints` dispatch bypassing the route composer, Play/Pause floating button auto-advances to the next junction or dead-end using camera yaw as the straightest tie-breaker, `osmRouteOverlayAttached` event mirrors the player↔route binding to gate FAB visibility + provide click-landed-on-route visual feedback) → `osm-route-overlay.mdc`
- **Sound NavMesh areas** (fixed-size radial zones, raycasting, cost sliders) → `sound-areas.mdc`
- **Navigation shortcuts** (elevators v1, dev-gated cross-floor hops; **two dev toggles**: "Use shortcuts" (gates everything) + "Prefer elevators" (always-lift-if-valid); strict-shortest by default, no slack; seat post-hop uses same `plan_route(section)` + `corridor_section` as non-shortcut seat nav with `floor_hint_y` / `branch_join_pos` branch rejoin; POI routes stay `plan_route_to_position` unless `corridorSection` added; USD `nav_shortcuts_layer.usda` + `shortcuts.json`, `ShortcutRouter`, `ShortcutTraversalService`, single-hop, known limitations) → `shortcuts.mdc`

